{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he believed in YHWH, and He counted it to him for righteousness.</b> Rashi explained (Rashi on Genesis 15:6): the Holy One, blessed be He, counted it to him as righteousness and merit on account of the faith that he believed in Him. But I do not understand what this merit is — why would he not believe in the El of truth, when he is himself a prophet, and not a man who lies? And one who believed to slaughter his beloved only son and [endured] the other trials — how would he not believe in good tidings? And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that it says that he believed in YHWH and considered that by virtue of the righteousness of the Holy One, blessed be He, He would give him seed in any case — not by virtue of Abram's own righteousness and reward, even though He said to him, \"your reward shall be very great.\" From this it follows that he would not fear lest sin cause [the promise to fail], for even though in the first prophecy he thought it would be conditional upon the reward for his deeds, now that He promised him he need not fear sin and that He would give him seed, he believed that the matter was assured from the side of Elohim — a truth that would not turn back, for it is the righteousness of YHWH, which admits no interruption, as it is written (Isaiah 45:23), \"By Myself have I sworn, says YHWH, the word has gone forth from My mouth in righteousness and shall not return.\" Alternatively, one may say that Abraham believed that he would in any case have seed to inherit, and the Holy One, blessed be He, further counted this promise — that He promised him — to him as righteousness, for by the righteousness of YHWH He would do so, as in \"Elohim meant it for good\" (Genesis 50:20), and likewise \"and it was counted to him for righteousness\" (Psalms 106:31), concerning Phinehas — that He counted to him this promise, in that he trusted in HaShem in that deed, as righteousness for generation to generation, for the El will forever keep it for him for the sake of His righteousness and His kindness, in the manner of \"forever I will keep for him My kindness\" (Psalms 89:29)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:29:34.661893081Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}